    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> When no cases were collected, the headless session just hangs, instead of terminating.\n\nThis is not *quite* a precise description of the problem, as \"headless session\" might be related to a child process from `new_child_neovim` or something else. In this case it seems to be the latter: if run from test is done from the CLI (like `make test`), then if there are no tests collected the reporter (which in this cases is responsible to closing the Neovim instance running 'mini.test') is not used.\n\nAlthough the current behavior is intentional, I think it might be reasonable to always go through reporter route. It will report that there are zero cases run instead of a custom message. I'll think about it a bit more.",
